  "scope": "One disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Kind cluster with the ready bundled, policy-capable kindnet CNI and one case-owned namespace. Two case-owned non-root Python DNS fixture Pods serve only the reserved .test name path.saf-0503-015.test over UDP and TCP on ports 5353 and 5354, returning only RFC 5737 TEST-NET-1/2 marker addresses. An exact selected client and an unselected comparator send ordinary DNS wire queries directly to those Pod IPs. The native Kubernetes NetworkPolicy permits the selected client only to the approved fixture Pod on UDP/TCP 5353. No public target, upstream forwarding, external DNS, host networking, privilege change, evasion, or data transfer is used. The case does not establish production CNI support, cluster-wide resolver configuration, NodeLocal DNSCache behavior, policy governance, or controls against node-local paths.",
